  // ── V4.1: data saver mode (§24.4.2, §23.1 point 5, §23.7 RL-8, §31.3 tier 4) ──
  //
  // Four requirements, all binding: visible state instead of a buried
  // setting; the consequence MUST be named ('datasaver_consequence' is
  // the translation of the sentence prescribed in the document 'less cover
  // traffic - this makes your node easier to recognize from outside'); the
  // app may SUGGEST, never activate by itself ('datasaver_suggest' says so
  // explicitly); and Secure is excluded without exception
  // ('datasaver_locked_secure' names the reason).
  //
  // §24.4.2 requires a CONTENT check for these texts, not just a
  // linguistic one: 'A translation that conceals the consequence undoes
  // exactly this rule - the 34 versions of this text must therefore be
  // checked for content, not only for language.' Each of the 34 versions of
  // 'datasaver_consequence' therefore names BOTH: less cover traffic AND
  // the easier recognisability from outside. The terms for 'cover
  // traffic' stem from 'secure_mode_explain_body' — the text that was
  // dropped with the send mode in S389 (§12.1); they were taken over so
  // that the same word stands for the same thing in every language, and
  // that continues to apply unchanged.
